        "patchSetId": 30
      },
      "lineNbr": 248,
      "author": {
        "id": 1112679
      },
      "writtenOn": "2024-12-19T12:35:33Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Most of the aggressive cases, there will be no connection update.\nAdded the comment about why it is here.\n\nThis check had to be here since we cannot check Hearing Aid activity in gd/, because it creates a dependency on stack/ code.",
      "parentUuid": "8e8772ca_d69d28b6",
      "revId": "7671e30bd7d5df176464d887002bb0d540c42ca9",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "402e00de_57c67bb8",
        "filename": "system/stack/l2cap/l2c_ble_conn_params.cc",
        "patchSetId": 30
      },
      "lineNbr": 248,
      "author": {
        "id": 1112679
      },
      "writtenOn": "2024-12-20T12:14:00Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "About this comment, do we want to use the 7.5ms interval for service discovery (as before), or we want to keep the initial aggressive parameters for it (set by system property, default by 10-20ms)? \n\nCurrent patch set is made for latter, but this may result slower service discovery than before. \n\n@okamil@google.com @jpawlowski@google.com What do you think?",
      "parentUuid": "f265c293_bbc06356",
      "revId": "7671e30bd7d5df176464d887002bb0d540c42ca9",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "c5a7b69f_98438bb8",
        "filename": "system/stack/l2cap/l2c_ble_conn_params.cc",
        "patchSetId": 30
      },
      "lineNbr": 248,
      "author": {
        "id": 1882530
      },
      "writtenOn": "2024-12-20T22:09:54Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Lets say we decide to switch parameters for service discovery.\n1. Initial parameters are aggressive. We can probably speed up service discovery even further by making the parameters even more aggressive. But I am not sure that we are going to see any significant improvement considering that the parameter update comes with its own time penaly.\n2. Initial parameters are relaxed. Relaxed parameters would have been choosen because of the bandwidth constraints. Switching to aggressive connection parameters would bring us back to the same problem that we were trying to avoid by using relaxed parameters.",
      "parentUuid": "402e00de_57c67bb8",
      "revId": "7671e30bd7d5df176464d887002bb0d540c42ca9",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889"
    },
